# Passkeys Sheet

::summary
The passkeys management sheet (F-14), opened from Settings → Account → Passkeys (2 passkeys · rpId surf.space): the enrolled credential rows (MacBook Pro, iPhone) with added/last-used meta and a trailing Remove, then Add passkey — the browser WebAuthn enrollment prompt.
::

::modal[name=passkeys title="Passkeys" width=340 placement=centered dismissible=true]

:::row[icon=login href=# trailing-label="Remove" trailing-action=removePasskey]
MacBook Pro
Added Jul 22, 2026 · last used today
:::

:::row[icon=device href=# trailing-label="Remove" trailing-action=removePasskey]
iPhone
Added Jul 22, 2026 · rpId surf.space
:::

:::toolbar
- button[label="Add passkey" action=addPasskey]
:::

::

Top-right ✕ per dismiss canon. Add passkey hands off to the browser's WebAuthn prompt; the new credential row appears on completion. Removing the last passkey warns before committing (password remains the fallback).

At small width (≤ 767px, R-C ruling 08-10) the sheet goes edge-to-edge with 10px side insets and auto width; the wide placement declared on the block is unchanged.
